All five findings fixed, gates re-run green.

**Findings and fixes**

1. **BLOCKER** — the matrix's skip was `member_resolves(module, builtin)`, derived from the table under audit. Now the skip list is `promised_by_the_documents()` (the `module.member` pairs the documents' code blocks write), skipped pairs are additionally asserted to be in `MODULE_MEMBERS`, and three counters are asserted to sum to the matrix size, so a new `continue` fails instead of hiding. Guard changed from `checked > BUILTIN_NAMES.len()` to `refused > promised_rows`.
2. **MAJOR** — `text.length`/`list.length` were answering with neither document writing them. Both documents now write *every* member of every module (`text.trim/contains/starts_with/ends_with/replace/length`, `math.abs/ceil/sin/cos/tan/log/exp`, `files.lines/delete/copy/rename`, `list.length`), and a new gate `edge_a_member_the_registry_holds_is_written_by_a_document` reads the table and asks **each** document. `filter`/`reduce` went the other way — out of the table, since a builtin nothing implements is not a member, matching `math.random`.
3. **MAJOR** — the matrix walked qualified `BUILTIN_NAMES`. `short_member_names()` now builds the universe from table members plus every short name behind a registered builtin: 11 × 64 = 704 pairs — **646 refused, 11 unparseable, 47 promised** — including `json.read`, `text.get`, `files.parse`.
4. **MINOR** — both engines now ask `module_has_member` before the `get_var(<module>_<member>)` hit, scoped to `stdlib::is_module` so a program's own `module … end` keeps its published members.
5. **MINOR** — the heading join-word is folded with `eq_ignore_ascii_case`.

Each fix was proven by reintroducing the defect (`csv` gaining `uppercase`, an open `module_has_member`, a registered `text_input` with the engine checks reverted, a deleted `text.length` doc line, `### JSON AND CSV`); real output is in `phases/phase-050/REPORT.md`. The new block-running assertions also caught two document defects: SPEC.md's single-quoted `json.parse('…')` (no single-quoted strings exist) and a line I had written with `has` as a variable.

**Gates**: fmt exit 0 · clippy `-D warnings` exit 0 · `cargo test --all-targets` 1430 passed / 0 failed / 0 ignored (53 lines) · `rb run` over 9 example+module files, 0 failures · `git status` has no stray artifacts.
